From: David Griego <dgriego@quicinc.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qrb2210-arduino-imola: reserve M-05 boundary window

Lab diagnostic only. UEFI advertises 0x7b8ff000-0x7c9fefff as conventional
memory while the bootloader memory fixup ends the bank at 0x7b8fefff. Pages
in this window raised synchronous external aborts during OSTree deployment
(UNO Q M-05). Keep the window out of the linear map and the allocator.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [lab diagnostic; not for upstream]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts
@@ -689,3 +689,16 @@
 &xo_board {
 	clock-frequency = <38400000>;
 };
+
+&reserved_memory {
+	/*
+	 * UNO Q M-05 lab diagnostic: UEFI advertises 0x7b8ff000-0x7c9fefff as
+	 * conventional RAM while the bootloader memory fixup ends the bank at
+	 * 0x7b8fefff. Pages here raised synchronous external aborts during
+	 * OSTree deployment. Keep the window out of the linear map/allocator.
+	 */
+	m05_boundary_guard: m05-boundary-guard@7b8ff000 {
+		reg = <0x0 0x7b8ff000 0x0 0x1100000>;
+		no-map;
+	};
+};
